<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,003.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,003.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, Oct 1 , Reuter - The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,003 today from 1,000 on Sep 30, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route			   Index    Rate    Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1   US GULF/ARA	  0994     9.029    0994     9.029</p>
<p>   1a  TRANSATLANTIC RV   0875  6629.000    0875  6629.000</p>
<p>   2   US GULF/JAPAN	1353    19.329    1351    19.307</p>
<p>   2a  SKAW P/USG/F EAST  1131  9721.000    1127  9243.000</p>
<p>   3   NOPAC/JAPAN	  1150    10.607    1148    10.593</p>
<p>   3a  JAPAN-SK/NOPAC/RV  0827  6529.000    0813  6414.000</p>
<p>   6   HR OR HR-RB/JAPAN  1105    11.400    1104    11.388</p>
<p>   7   HR/ROTTERDAM	 1017     4.950    1017     4.950</p>
<p>   8   QLAND/ROTTERDAM    0712     7.825    0711     7.819</p>
